---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// Keep this in sync with app/legal/terms.tsx.
const updated = '27 July 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of service — Plinth"
  description="The terms governing use of the Plinth recipe app, including subscriptions, acceptable use, and disclaimers."
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Terms of service</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>Welcome</h2>
      <p>
        These terms govern your use of Plinth. By creating an account or using the app, you agree
        to them. If you don't agree, please don't use the app.
      </p>
      <p>
        Operator: Shawn Masule (Namibia)<br />
        Contact: <a href="mailto:plinthrecipes@gmail.com">plinthrecipes@gmail.com</a>
      </p>

      <h2>Your account</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You must be at least 13 years old to use Plinth.</li>
        <li>
          Keep your sign-in credentials secure. You're responsible for activity on your account.
        </li>
        <li>
          We may suspend or close accounts that violate these terms, attempt fraud, or harm other
          users.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Free trial</h2>
      <p>
        New accounts get free access to Plinth Premium for the first 21 days. After the trial
        ends, premium features are locked unless you subscribe. The trial does not auto-charge —
        you only pay if you actively choose to subscribe.
      </p>

      <h2>Subscription and billing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Plinth Premium is a paid subscription billed through our payment processor. Pricing is
          shown at checkout in your local currency.
        </li>
        <li>
          Subscriptions auto-renew at the end of each billing period unless cancelled. We'll renew
          at the same price you signed up at.
        </li>
        <li>
          You can cancel any time from the Premium tab. You keep access until the end of the
          current billing period.
        </li>
        <li>
          Refunds are at our discretion. Email us if you believe a charge was made in error.
        </li>
        <li>
          We may change pricing for new sign-ups. Existing subscribers stay on the price they
          signed up at until they cancel.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Recipe content</h2>
      <p>
        Recipes shown in Plinth are sourced from third-party providers and the original
        publishers. We don't guarantee accuracy, nutritional precision, or suitability for medical
        conditions or allergies. Always check ingredients yourself before cooking, especially if
        you have dietary restrictions.
      </p>

      <h2>Dietitian plan disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        Plinth is not a medical service. Calorie and macro suggestions are rough estimates based
        on standard formulas, not personalised medical advice. Consult a qualified dietitian or
        physician before making significant dietary changes, especially if you have a health
        condition.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>Don't use Plinth to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Violate any law or another person's rights.</li>
        <li>Reverse engineer, scrape, or copy the app or its data.</li>
        <li>Attempt to gain unauthorised access to the service or other accounts.</li>
        <li>Resell access or share your account with others.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The Plinth name, brand, code, and design are owned by us. You may use the app for
        personal, non-commercial purposes. Recipe content and images displayed in-app remain the
        property of their original creators and are shown for personal cooking purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>App store rules</h2>
      <p>
        If you downloaded Plinth from the App Store or Play Store, your use is also subject to
        their terms. Apple and Google are third-party beneficiaries of these terms with the right
        to enforce them.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        Plinth is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind. We are not liable for any
        indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or loss of profits,
        data, or use, arising from your use of the app. Some jurisdictions don't allow these
        exclusions, so they may not apply to you.
      </p>

      <h2>Termination</h2>
      <p>
        You may stop using Plinth at any time. We may terminate or suspend your access if you
        breach these terms. On termination, your right to use the app ends, but sections that by
        their nature should survive termination (intellectual property, limitation of liability,
        outstanding subscription charges) will continue to apply.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms when we add features, change services, or comply with new laws.
        If we make material changes, we'll notify you in-app or by email. Continuing to use Plinth
        after changes take effect means you accept the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Namibia. Disputes will be resolved
        in Namibian courts.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms:
        <a href="mailto:plinthrecipes@gmail.com">plinthrecipes@gmail.com</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
